{
  "question_text": "You are given a dataset of **Yelp businesses**. Identify the **top 5 cities** with the highest number of **5-star rated businesses**, including both open and closed businesses.\r\n\r\nIf two or more cities have the same number of 5-star businesses, assign them the **same rank** and skip the next rank accordingly (e.g., if two cities tie for 1st, the next city is ranked 3rd).\r\n\r\n**Input DataFrame:** `yelp_business`\r\n\r\n| Column Name  | Type    |\r\n| ------------ | ------- |\r\n| business_id  | object  |\r\n| name         | object  |\r\n| neighborhood | object  |\r\n| address      | object  |\r\n| city         | object  |\r\n| state        | object  |\r\n| postal_code  | object  |\r\n| latitude     | float64 |\r\n| longitude    | float64 |\r\n| stars        | float64 |\r\n| review_count | int64   |\r\n| is_open      | int64   |\r\n| categories   | object  |\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary style=\"padding:8px 16px; background-color:#2196F3; color:white; border-radius:4px; cursor:pointer; display:inline-block; list-style:none;\">Preview Input Data</summary>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n|business\\_id|name|neighborhood|address|city|state|postal\\_code|latitude|longitude|stars|review\\_count|is\\_open|categories|\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n|OZC42gnhlJ\\_auXduDRfMoQ|Scratch||1011 N 3rd St|Phoenix|AZ|85004|33\\.46|-112\\.07|3\\.0|40\\.0|0\\.0|French;Restaurants|\r\n|Lhtl6hEr4BaAR4aA3RQDNQ|Dairy Queen||475 W Craig Rd|North Las Vegas|NV|89032|36\\.24|-115\\.15|2\\.0|57\\.0|1\\.0|Food;Ice Cream & Frozen Yogurt|\r\n|xl8jk0FbszttHyI\\_vjozkA|Ton V Lee, DDS|Southeast|2425 E Hacienda Ave, Ste 120, Summerlin Smiles|Las Vegas|NV|89120|36\\.09|-115\\.12|5\\.0|4\\.0|1\\.0|Health & Medical;Dentists;Cosmetic Dentists;General Dentistry|\r\n|CX8pfLn7Bk9o2-8yDMp\\_2w|The UPS Store||4815 E Carefree Hwy, Ste 108|Cave Creek|AZ|85331|33\\.8|-111\\.98|1\\.5|5\\.0|1\\.0|Notaries;Printing Services;Local Services;Shipping Centers|\r\n|xxCrRqqICzQyR0Q-iqCrNw|Subway|Plaza Midwood|1300 The Plz|Charlotte|NC|28205|35\\.22|-80\\.81|2\\.0|13\\.0|1\\.0|Fast Food;Sandwiches;Restaurants|\r\n|Wvst5nUM1Yd64cdjIPOD6w|Alima's Roti and Pastry|Malton|13 Kenview Boulevard, Unit 49|Brampton|ON|L6T 5K9|43\\.74|-79\\.65|4\\.0|19\\.0|1\\.0|Food;Caribbean;Specialty Food;Restaurants;Indian|\r\n|mRDyt98UXamjbSOX9NinlA|Juniper Branch Library||1825 West Union Hills Dr|Phoenix|AZ|85027|33\\.65|-112\\.1|4\\.0|16\\.0|1\\.0|Libraries;Public Services & Government|\r\n|yzAB\\_pRwk8FJl3aILiiySA|CenturyLink|Spring Valley|4850 S Fort Apache Rd, Ste 100|Las Vegas|NV|89147|36\\.1|-115\\.3|1\\.5|35\\.0|0\\.0|Home Services;Television Service Providers;Professional Services;Internet Service Providers;Utilities|\r\n|4m5g6GUGDN9NqkfA0dk9fA|Test America Preview Studios|The Strip|3667 Las Vegas Blvd S, Ste H-82, Desert Passage Mall at the Aladdin|Las Vegas|NV|89109|36\\.11|-115\\.17|3\\.0|10\\.0|1\\.0|Arts & Entertainment;Local Services|\r\n|RtcVbq18T0vNODpGwHzcVQ|Standard Restaurant Supply||5675 S Valley View|Las Vegas|NV|89118|36\\.09|-115\\.19|3\\.5|20\\.0|1\\.0|Kitchen & Bath;Shopping;Home & Garden;Restaurant Supplies;Professional Services;Wholesalers|\r\n|PmLFk1s8pPVNXChqETM4MA|Coco Lezzone|The Annex|137 Avenue Road|Toronto|ON|M5R 2H4|43\\.67|-79\\.4|5\\.0|17\\.0|0\\.0|Italian;Restaurants;Event Planning & Services;Caterers|\r\n|YiaOpyu4qx0x1nJC\\_G33TQ|Grimaldi's Pizzeria||7131 West Ray Rd, Ste 23|Chandler|AZ|85226|33\\.32|-111\\.97|4\\.0|187\\.0|1\\.0|Pizza;Restaurants|\r\n|Ch7Kx4JPJePFvjpXw0PAVQ|AliKat Photography|||Gilbert|AZ|85234|33\\.37|-111\\.75|5\\.0|12\\.0|1\\.0|Photographers;Event Photography;Session Photography;Event Planning & Services|\r\n\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n**Requirements**\r\n\r\n- Filter businesses with exactly 5-star rating\r\n- Include both open and closed businesses\r\n- Count the number of 5-star businesses per city\r\n- Rank cities using dense ranking (ties share the same rank, next rank is skipped)\r\n- Return only the top 5 ranked cities\r\n- Use the provided `yelp_business` DataFrame as-is, do not modify or reconstruct the dataset\r\n\r\n**Returns**\r\n\r\n- `pandas.DataFrame` with columns:\r\n  - `rank`: Rank of the city (ties share same rank)\r\n  - `city`: Name of the city\r\n  - `total_5_star_businesses`: Number of 5-star businesses in that city",
  "short_text": "Top 5 Cities by 5-Star Businesses",
  "difficulty": "EASY",
  "function_name": "top_cities_five_star",
  "param_names": [
    "yelp_business"
  ],
  "starter_code": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef top_cities_five_star(yelp_business):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identify the top 5 cities with the highest number of 5-star rated businesses.\n    Use dense ranking for ties.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Your code here\n    return",
  "solution_code": "import pandas as pd\ndef top_cities_five_star(yelp_business):\n    five = yelp_business[yelp_business[\"stars\"] == 5.0]\n    counts = five.groupby(\"city\").size().reset_index(name=\"total_5_star_businesses\")\n    counts[\"rank\"] = counts[\"total_5_star_businesses\"].rank(method=\"dense\", ascending=False).astype(int)\n    counts = counts[counts[\"rank\"] <= 5].sort_values([\"rank\", \"city\"]).reset_index(drop=True)\n    return counts[[\"rank\", \"city\", \"total_5_star_businesses\"]]",
  "language": "PYTHON38_DATASCIENCE",
  "time_limit": 4.0,
  "rounding": 4,
  "library": "pandas",
